.TH BLURCAM 1 "October 2026" "BlurCam 0.1.0"
.SH NAME
blurcam \- local face privacy and camera effects
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B blurcam
[global options] command [command options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Native Linux face detection, optical-flow tracking and ROI effects.
No telemetry or cloud processing. Only explicit model installation uses the network.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B file INPUT OUTPUT
Process MP4, MKV or WebM. INPUT may be stdin (-). OUTPUT may also be supplied
with -o. Stdout (-) produces streaming MKV. Copies compatible audio and preserves
video timestamps. Incompatible audio fails instead of being silently dropped.
.TP
.B preview
Display the filtered webcam in an SDL window.
.TP
.B webcam
Preview webcam or supply --output - for raw BGR24. --no-preview requires output.
.TP
.B virtualcam
Write YUYV to existing v4l2loopback (default /dev/video10). --preview shows a window.
.TP
.B devices
List accessible V4L2 names, formats, resolutions and frame intervals.
.TP
.B effects [NAME]
List effects, descriptions and parameters.
.TP
.B models install | list
Install checksum-pinned MIT YuNet or inspect installation status.
.TP
.B benchmark
Synthetic stage timing; --resolution WIDTHxHEIGHT, --fps N, --frames N.
.TP
.B info
Show library versions and CPU/CUDA/encoder capabilities.
.TP
.B completions bash | zsh | fish
Emit basic shell completion.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --effect NAME[,NAME...]
Ordered effect stack; option may be repeated.
.TP
.B --preset NAME
privacy, max-privacy, anonymous, cyberpunk, glitch, VHS, subtle, medium, chaos.
.TP
.B --config PATH, --profile NAME, --save-config PATH
TOML options. Precedence: defaults, global TOML, built-in preset, user profile, CLI.
Saving refuses overwrite.
.TP
.B --backend auto|cpu|cuda
Detector inference backend. GPU effects/decode are not implemented.
.TP
.B --device PATH_OR_NAME
Camera path or exact friendly name (live modes only).
.TP
.B --input PATH
Paced file replay for live modes, without accessing a camera.
.TP
.B --width N, --height N, --fps N
Requested live camera format.
.TP
.B --limit-frames N
Bound a live session. Zero runs until EOF, quit or signal.
.TP
.B --confidence F, --detection-interval N, --detector-size N, --max-faces N
Score threshold, refresh period, max detector side, detection capacity.
.TP
.B --tracking-smoothing F, --padding F
Previous coordinate weight and expansion fraction per side.
.TP
.B --faces all|largest|ID, --mask box|ellipse
Face selection and mask. Selective/ellipse modes can expose faces or box corners.
.TP
.B --privacy-failsafe, --no-privacy-failsafe
Opaque covering on detected uncertainty. Two detection confirmations permit recovery.
.TP
.B --failsafe-mode full-frame|upper-body|last-known-region|expanded-face
Full-frame is default. Regional modes provide weaker protection.
.TP
.B --blur-radius N, --blur-type gaussian|box, --pixel-size N
Blur kernel width (rounded to odd) and mosaic block width.
.TP
.B --seed N, --image PATH
Effect RNG seed and RGBA overlay image.
.TP
.B --codec auto|h264|h265|vp9|av1|ffv1|h264_nvenc|hevc_nvenc|av1_nvenc
File encoder. Auto selects software H.264 or VP9 for WebM.
.TP
.B --overwrite
Explicit atomic replacement of file output. Input and output must differ.
.TP
.B --quiet, --verbose, --debug, --threads N
Logs, backend details, visible debug annotations, worker count.
.SH PREVIEW KEYS
q/Escape quit; 1 blur; 2 pixelate; 3 glitch; 4 censor; 5 VHS;
[ and ] adjust strength; f FPS title; d/t debug boxes (including simultaneous outputs).
.SH PRIVACY
No detector guarantees anonymity. A never-detected face can remain visible while
another face is tracked. Use opaque censoring, box masks, detection interval 1 and
full-frame fail-safe for conservative use. Review all sensitive recordings.
Regional fail-safe modes and decorative effects are not equivalent protection.
.SH FILES
~/.config/blurcam/config.toml; ~/.local/share/blurcam/models/yunet-2023mar.onnx.
XDG_CONFIG_HOME and XDG_DATA_HOME override the roots.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success, 1 runtime failure, CLI parser-specific nonzero errors, 130 interrupted pipeline.
.SH SEE ALSO
ffmpeg(1), v4l2-ctl(1)
